{"beat": 6, "name": "WHAT TO DO", "text": "This week. First, pick your top products and pull price and units by month, as far back as you have. Next, plot them and fit the line: log of units against log of price. The slope is the elasticity, and the spreadsheet gives you the standard error beside it. If the price never moved, you have no line, and the first job is to move it, in small steps, both ways, and wait 5 months. Then compute your true unit margin, after the platform and the ads, not the gross one, and put the price where the fraction you keep equals the inverse of the slope. Last, take the step as a step, not a leap. Cap it, read the result against the range, and go again.", "provider": "library", "words": [{"word": "This", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.255}, {"word": "week.", "start": 0.325, "end": 0.882}, {"word": "First,", "start": 1.695, "end": 2.322}, {"word": "pick", "start": 2.438, "end": 2.647}, {"word": "your", "start": 2.682, "end": 2.786}, {"word": "top", "start": 2.821, "end": 3.019}, {"word": "products", "start": 3.077, "end": 3.437}, {"word": "and", "start": 3.471, "end": 3.541}, {"word": "pull", "start": 3.587, "end": 3.785}, {"word": "price", "start": 3.866, "end": 4.145}, {"word": "and", "start": 4.191, "end": 4.319}, {"word": "units", "start": 4.4, "end": 4.644}, {"word": "by", "start": 4.69, "end": 4.783}, {"word": "month,", "start": 4.853, "end": 5.143}, {"word": "as", "start": 5.166, "end": 5.283}, {"word": "far", "start": 5.352, "end": 5.526}, {"word": "back", "start": 5.584, "end": 5.77}, {"word": "as", "start": 5.817, "end": 5.886}, {"word": "you", "start": 5.921, "end": 6.002}, {"word": "have.", "start": 6.072, "end": 6.606}, {"word": "Next,", "start": 6.931, "end": 7.407}, {"word": "plot", "start": 7.523, "end": 7.79}, {"word": "them", "start": 7.837, "end": 7.976}, {"word": "and", "start": 8.022, "end": 8.104}, {"word": "fit", "start": 8.162, "end": 8.313}, {"word": "the", "start": 8.348, "end": 8.417}, {"word": "line:", "start": 8.464, 